":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.7.dev [a8643700ce8affae9fed0d2688b9f7867f5b7d4e]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev (a8643700c) - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9602) - AMD Ryzen 9 9900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 61.66 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nGLES3 scene forward fragment shader compilation fails when running web export in Chrome with WebGL 2.0 backend.\n The error occurs due to mixed int/float type operations that desktop OpenGL drivers accept through implicit\nconversion, but WebGL 2.0 (ANGLE) strictly rejects according to GLSL ES 3.00 specification.\n\n<img width=\"638\" height=\"236\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f40b0594-2931-4ee1-a2e1-012a685d3037\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create any Godot 4.7 project with Compatibility renderer (uses WebGL 2.0 by default)\n2. Export to Web with default settings\n3. Run in Chrome browser (uses ANGLE for WebGL)\n4. Open Developer Tools console to see the shader compilation errors\n5. The browser may display a black/broken screen due to failed shader compilation\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n- [mcp-shader-error.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26828361/mcp-shader-error.zip)\n- https://shiena.github.io/mcp-shader-error/","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_